<title>ITALY: Olivetti trade resumes after suspension.</title>
<headline>Olivetti trade resumes after suspension.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Olivetti shares sank further when trading resumed after the stock had been suspended at the 10 percent limit down for most of the morning.</p>
<p>Olivetti was quoted at 485 lire, a fall of 12.55 percent on the day, at 1100 gmt after trading bands were widened to 15 percent.</p>
<p>Shares plunged after the company announced a capital write-down plan on the back of heavy losses in 1996 and the first quarter of 1997.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392-66102321</p>
